---
title: Overview
description: What the document library holds, how it is arranged, and how to find a file.
sidebar:
  order: 1
---

The document library keeps your firm's files in one place: the documents of each client company, the files of each case, and the firm's own internal documents. Select **Documents** in the left side bar to open it.

## The three areas

The folder tree on the left always has three top-level areas:

| Area | What it holds |
|---|---|
| **Client Docs** | One folder tree for each client company. Expand **Client Docs**, then a company. If the list is long, use **Search companies…**, or **Load more** at the end of the list. |
| **Cases** | One folder tree for each case that is assigned to you or that you created, newest first. CRM opportunities that have files are listed here too. |
| **Internal Docs** | The firm's own documents — policies, templates, internal records. |

Select **Client Docs** or **Cases** to expand it, then select a company or a case. **Internal Docs** can be selected directly.

{% aside type="note" %}
The files of a case are under **Cases**, not under the client company. The exception is bookkeeping: documents uploaded in the bookkeeping workbench are filed in the company's **ACCOUNTS & TAX** folder under **Client Docs**.
{% /aside %}

## Folders created by Operon

Some folders are created for you:

| Where | Folders |
|---|---|
| A new client company | **ACCOUNTS & TAX**, **BILLS**, **INCORP**, **MARKETING**, **SECRETARY** and **VIP**. You can rename or delete them. |
| A company's books | Under **ACCOUNTS & TAX**: **Account** (with a folder for each financial year and month), **GST** (a folder for each quarter), **Tax** and **FS**. These are kept by Operon and cannot be renamed, moved or deleted. |
| A case | Folders that the case's workflow creates when it files something, such as **Client materials**, **Generated**, **Signed**, **Superseded**, **Filings** and **Payments**. They cannot be renamed, moved or deleted. Signed copies are filed in **Signed** by the signing step; you cannot upload into it. |

Files that a workflow created are marked **From workflow**. If such a file is locked, point at the ⓘ next to it to see why.

## The file list

The middle of the page shows the folders and files of what you selected: folders first, then files, 50 to a page. The columns are **Name**, **Owner** (who uploaded the file) and **Modified**. A file marked **Sensitive** is a highly sensitive document (see [Who can see what](/en/documents/access/#sensitive-documents)).

**Recent** in the left panel lists the last files you opened in this browser.

## Find a file

Type in **Search documents…** at the top of the left panel. The search looks for file names in the area you have selected — the company, the case or **Internal Docs** — not across the whole library. Select an area first, then search.

